course: dictionary
lesson: 7619
title: Pro: one short word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Pro is a short word, and it can mean different things. The context tells you which meaning to choose. «Being a pro is mostly the boring parts done for years: practice, sleep, planned food, rest days, physio after injuries.» The long list of practice and rest shows that a pro is a person paid to play a sport or do a job, and that it takes years of hard work.
explain: Pro can also mean very good at something. Lily says, «You're a pro at this!» She is not saying you are paid. She means you are very skilled. Check it by swapping in your meaning: "You're very good at this!" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Pro has another use at school. «Pros and cons» are the reasons for and against something. Before a class vote, you might list the pros and cons of a plan, then decide. When you meet a new word like pro, ask: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still works.
fact: Pro is short for professional, a person who is paid to do a sport or job.
fact: «Pros and cons» means the reasons for and the reasons against something.
fact: The prefix pro- means in favour of, as in pro-environment.
fact: «Like a pro» means doing something very well, as if you have had lots of practice.
fact: «Turn pro» means to start being paid for a sport.
exercise: «Being a pro is mostly the boring parts done for years.» In this sentence, what is a pro? | *A person who is paid to do a sport or job | A person who is very tired | A kind of healthy food | A reason for something
exercise: Lily says, «You're a pro at this!» What does pro mean here? | Someone who never plays | *Very good at something | A reason for and against something | A kind of football boot
exercise: Your teacher asks you to list the «pros and cons» of a new park. What are the pros? | *The reasons in favour of the park | The hours the park is open | The reasons against the park | The names of the people in the debate
test: A group that is pro-environment wants to: | Build more roads through the park | Ban all cars in the city | Sell the trees for wood | *Help and protect the environment
test: «Jake decided to turn pro at sixteen.» What does turn pro mean here? | Stop playing his sport for ever | *Start being paid to play his sport | Become a teacher of sport | Win a prize at school
exam: Which sentence uses pro to mean a reason for something? | Lily is a pro at chess | Jake turned pro last year | She was a pro footballer for ten years | *We listed the pros and cons before we chose a plan
